# Design system

Dark charcoal is the default. The look is a calm SaaS surface with a cyberpunk signal: orange light on a near-black field, not a neon grid.

Use semantic tokens. Do not hard-code hex unless no token exists.

- `bg-background` / `text-foreground` — canvas and body (`#0B0B0D` / `#F8FAFC`)
- `bg-card` / `bg-secondary` — panels (`#1F2937`)
- `text-muted-foreground` — secondary text, inactive icons (`#6B7280`)
- `bg-primary` / `ring` — actions, active state, focus (`#FF7A1A`)
- `text-primary-foreground` — label on orange (`#0B0B0D`)

Orange is for buttons, links, focus, and a soft glow. Do not fill large surfaces with it. Headings use `font-display` (Space Grotesk). Body stays `font-sans` (Inter).

```tsx
// BAD
<button className="bg-[#FF7A1A] text-white">Join</button>

// GOOD
<button className="bg-primary text-primary-foreground shadow-[0_0_24px_color-mix(in_srgb,var(--primary)_35%,transparent)]">
  Join
</button>
<h1 className="font-display text-foreground">Build</h1>
```
